commit 7303179c36ccdd99c13d3913775ff8cc2b71769a
Author: Alex Yang <agegcn@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 30 19:40:57 2026 +0800

    fix(chat): branch a history edit only when it is sent (#1009)
    
    * fix(chat): branch a history edit only when it is sent
    
    "Edit from here" called navigate_tree on click, which persisted a leaf
    move before the user committed to the edit. There was no way back, and
    a reload showed the conversation cut off at the edited message (#958).
    
    Clicking now only prefills the composer and records the target entry in
    useAgentSession. The composer shows an edit banner with Cancel, which
    clears the prefill without touching the session. Sending navigates first
    and then takes the normal prompt path; a failed navigation restores the
    draft and the edit state. The pending edit follows the session's
    in-memory draft across session switches, and a pending edit is never
    sent as steer or follow-up.
    
    Navigation and prompt remain two RPCs, so a prompt rejected after the
    navigation keeps the new leaf.
    
    * fix(chat): expose history edit actions on touch screens
    
    * revert(chat): keep user-message actions on hover for touch screens
    
    Always showing Copy / Edit from here / New session at 44px under every
    user message on phones is a separate design change from deferring the
    history-edit branch, and it costs a lot of vertical space per turn. A tap
    on the message already reveals the actions (mobile browsers emulate
    mouseenter on tap), so leave that layout as it is here.
    
    This reverts commit 8931c5a99dc33fec4295ea43f52f925a08e028f6.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
